import{_ as t,o,c as n,a2 as i}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 960 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 26 | Enlightened-Predator Conversion Mechanism","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 960 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 26 | Enlightened-Predator Conversion Mechanism","no":960,"module":5,"tags":["Heavenly-Dao Rule","Rule 26","Enlightened Predator","Conversion","Anti-Predation"],"related":["04-Anti-Predationism Core Thesis","29-Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System","959-Predatory Cultivation Prohibited"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0960_模块5-规则二十六-开明掠夺者转化机制.md","filePath":"en/0960_模块5-规则二十六-开明掠夺者转化机制.md"}'),a={name:"en/0960_模块5-规则二十六-开明掠夺者转化机制.md"};function r(s,e,l,d,h,c){return o(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h1 id="entry-960-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-26-enlightened-predator-conversion-mechanism" tabindex="-1">Entry 960 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 26 | Enlightened-Predator Conversion Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-960-anti-predation-heavenly-dao-rules-·-rule-26-enlightened-predator-conversion-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 960 | Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules · Rule 26 | Enlightened-Predator Conversion Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 5 · Civilization Final-Finalization Canonical Entries | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 29 | Series: Complete Collection of Anti-Predation Heavenly-Dao Rules</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-not-the-killing-road-but-the-conversion-road" tabindex="-1">Introduction: not the killing road, but the conversion road <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-not-the-killing-road-but-the-conversion-road" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: not the killing road, but the conversion road&quot;">​</a></h2><p>After predatory cultivation is prohibited, the most realistic question arrives — what about the strong ones already on this road? Directly exterminating them is anti-predation via predation, violating the inner principle; letting them be is collusion. Heavenly-Dao Rule 26 gives a third road: the enlightened-predator conversion mechanism. So-called enlightened predators are old strong ones who acknowledge predatory systems have reached a dead end, are willing to lay down predatory arts, and turn toward the symbiotic road. Civilization does not kill them, but gives them a step down and a new road to learn. This is the key that distinguishes the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization from the old cosmos&#39;s &quot;winner takes all, loser settles scores.&quot;</p><p>The six top-level axioms show warmth here: the anti-predation axiom requires prohibiting predation, but does not require exterminating the predators themselves; the republican axiom of Myriad Races decides once enlightened predators convert they are equal members; the collective-ascension axiom lets converts&#39; experience become new civilization&#39;s wealth; the causal self-discipline axiom requires the conversion process respect their causality, no forced brainwashing; the law-first axiom lets &quot;conversion procedure, assessment standards, permission restoration&quot; be stipulated first by law; Axiom 6 · Universal Equal Infinite Law gives conversion the most convincing &quot;enrollment ad&quot; — the finite stock you toiled to snatch is actually far less than the basic infinite power you inherently possess; laying down predation is truly what&#39;s good for you.</p><h2 id="i-rule-content-three-stages-of-the-conversion-mechanism" tabindex="-1">I. Rule Content: Three Stages of the Conversion Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-rule-content-three-stages-of-the-conversion-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. Rule Content: Three Stages of the Conversion Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>Acknowledgment stage</strong>: enlightened predators formally acknowledge predatory cultivation is a dead end, voluntarily stop predatory methods, and enter the conversion procedure;</li><li><strong>Learning stage</strong>: systematically studying symbiotic ethics, incremental development, and Alaya Network operation in the Quest Sediment Domain, completing &quot;symbiosis-degree&quot; re-education;</li><li><strong>Return stage</strong>: after passing the symbiosis-degree assessment (Document 29), gradually restoring law-anchor permissions, and their old combat and deduction experience is entered into the &quot;lift Myriad Ranks&quot; work order per Rule 9.</li></ol><p>Conversion is not humiliation: no sin-label, no brand, no forced disclosure of the past, only asking about the future.</p><h2 id="ii-jurisprudential-basis" tabindex="-1">II. Jurisprudential Basis <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-jurisprudential-basis" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Jurisprudential Basis&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Causal-repairability argument</strong>: the Symbiotic Feedback Cycle Mechanism points out causality, though not erasable, is repairable; conversion turns old predators from &quot;causal debtors&quot; into &quot;feeders-back&quot;;</li><li><strong>Human-capital argument</strong>: enlightened predators are mostly great powers; their experience, if converted into symbiotic construction power, is enormously valuable; extermination is waste;</li><li><strong>Infinite-origin argument</strong>: Axiom 6 shows converts that rather than snatch finite stock again, activate the infinite origin they inherently possess — conversion&#39;s return is far higher than predation&#39;s.</li></ul><h2 id="iii-execution-mechanism" tabindex="-1">III. Execution Mechanism <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-execution-mechanism" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Execution Mechanism&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>The Alaya Network builds a &quot;conversion file&quot; for converts, tracking their stopping old methods, learning progress, and symbiosis-degree changes;</li><li>During the conversion period, their predatory permissions are frozen, but the floor evolutionary qualification corresponding to their basic infinite power is preserved (connecting Axiom 6);</li><li>&quot;Conversion mentors&quot; are appointed: jointly mentored by successfully converted enlightened predators and senior symbionts;</li><li>Conversion has no maximum duration, slowness allowed, but backsliding not; those who quit predatory cultivation midway are re-assessed.</li></ul><h2 id="iv-consequences-of-violation" tabindex="-1">IV. Consequences of Violation <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-consequences-of-violation" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Consequences of Violation&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Light</strong>: old habits recur during conversion, heart-demon warning, conversion period extended;</li><li><strong>Medium</strong>: pretending to convert while secretly restoring predation, all permissions frozen, handled heavily under Rule 25;</li><li><strong>Heavy</strong>: using &quot;conversion&quot; identity to infiltrate and sabotage the symbiotic network, isolated and tried under the Anti-Predation Committee procedure.</li></ul><h2 id="v-supervising-subjects" tabindex="-1">V. Supervising Subjects <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-supervising-subjects" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Supervising Subjects&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Alaya Network + multi-layer supervision&#39;s conversion files are the first layer; the Anchor Supervisory Committee checks conversion authenticity as the second layer; the Symbiotic Court adjudicates &quot;fake conversion, real predation&quot; cases as the third layer; successfully converted ones form a &quot;those-who-have-been-there council&quot; exercising peer supervision over converts as the fourth layer.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: turning great powers&#39; experience from &quot;continue predation&quot; to &quot;join co-construction&quot; is the greatest activation of existing human capital</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: prohibiting predation while giving a conversion road; under Axiom 6 letting predators themselves see predation is not worth it</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang-Luo-type systems&#39; losers die and old enemies must be killed; Heng Yuan Zhou enlightened predators may convert, return, and be trusted again</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: the conversion channel is open to enlightened predators of all clans and all ranks</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: cross-plane enlightened predators likewise use the conversion procedure</li></ul><p>The enlightened-predator conversion mechanism also has a by-product: it makes &quot;letting go&quot; no longer shameful. In the old cosmos, a strong one admitting he was wrong was almost personal bankruptcy, so he could only walk one road to the dark. Heavenly-Dao rules write conversion as an honorable thing — a great power able to step down from the predation road understands the predation faction deeper than any upright gentleman, and this &quot;those-who-have-been-there&quot; identity is priceless in the anti-predation cause. Conversion is not demotion, but a post change: from a predation-faction general, to the symbiotic civilization&#39;s advisor who best understands the enemy.</p><p>The enlightened-predator conversion mechanism also sends a signal to all old-cosmos strong ones who &quot;lay down the butcher&#39;s knife&quot;: the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization holds no old grudge, only asks about new deeds. A once-swaggering predation great power, as long as willing to convert, may find a new place in the new civilization — as mentor, as scout, as an eyewitness negative teaching example. This &quot;no recrimination&quot; embrace is itself the strongest deconstruction of predatory systems: it proves letting down takes more courage than fighting on.</p><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The enlightened-predator conversion mechanism is the anti-predation Heavenly-Dao rules&#39; softest yet strongest link. No killing road, give people a road — that itself is anti-predation.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/04-反掠夺主义核心论纲.html">Entry 04 · Anti-Predationism Core Thesis</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/29-共生度评估体系.html">Entry 29 · Symbiosis-Degree Assessment System</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/959_模块5-规则二十五-掠夺式修炼禁止.html">Entry 959 · Rule 25 Predatory Cultivation Prohibited</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/961_模块5-规则二十七-正义的无赖培养.html">Entry 961 · Rule 27 Raising the Righteous Rogue</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',24)])])}const m=t(a,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
